  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}.$",
  "worked_solution": "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{4}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{u}_{4}(t)} & =\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{{u}_{4}(t)}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}} \\\\ {u}_{4}(t) & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{{e}^{-4s}}{s}} & ={u}_{4}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
